<title>USA: Group files complaint against Teamsters union.</title>
<headline>Group files complaint against Teamsters union.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A legal group said on Thursday it filed a complaint against the Teamsters union for allegedly misinforming striking United Parcel Service workers about their right to resign from the union.</p>
<p>&quot;The Teamsters officials are guilty of lying to employees,&quot; National Right to Work Legal Defense Foundation President Reed Larson said after the group filed its complaint with the National Labor Relations Board.</p>
<p>The Teamsters union denied the charges and questioned the group's motives. &quot;They have a history of trying to help corporations bust and weaken unions,&quot; Teamsters spokeswoman Gaye Williams said.</p>
<p>((Washington newsroom, 202 898-8300))</p>
